///1ASM86
Help by Willem Aandewiel
ASM86 - Assemble 8086 and 8088 source for CP/M-86

Use ASM86 to translate .A86 source into .H86 machine-code records.
Use GENCMD afterwards to create the executable .CMD file.

///2SYNTAX
  A>ASM86 HELP

The default source extension is .A86.
With the tools on A: and source on B:, for example:

  B>A:ASM86 HELP

///2FILES
  HELP.A86   Assembly source: edit this file.
  HELP.H86   Hexadecimal output: input to GENCMD.
  HELP.LST   Assembly listing, including diagnostic messages.
  HELP.SYM   Symbol information.

HELP.NAS, if present in the HELP package, is for NASM on a modern
host. It is not the source to give to ASM86.

///2BUILDING
For the supplied HELP.A86, use:

  A>ASM86 HELP
  A>GENCMD HELP
  A>HELP

Run GENCMD only after correcting all assembler errors.

///2ERRORS
Inspect HELP.LST and the assembler's messages.
Correct HELP.A86, then assemble again.
A generated H86 file alone does not prove a successful assembly.

///2OPTIONS
Optional assembler parameters follow a dollar sign:

  ASM86 filename $parameters

Use the ASM-86 Programmer's Guide for the installed version.
The supplied HELP.A86 needs no additional assembler parameters.
